Halloween (Allehelgensaften) is here or coming up in Denmark — marked on October 31, though it's a newer, imported tradition that not everyone celebrates.

Where it's celebrated, expect costumes, carved pumpkins, and children going door to door for candy (saying "slik eller ballade!"). Even households that don't dress up often keep some candy on hand for the kids who come by.

